# Security headers for the whole site. Netlify applies these to every
# response matching the path pattern, on top of (not instead of) whatever
# _redirects proxies through — see that file for the /api/* -> Azure rule.
#
# CSP is scoped to what the app actually loads: same-origin scripts/styles/
# fonts/images, plus the cookieless analytics provider and the Sentry ingest
# endpoint. Google Tag Manager and Google Analytics used to be listed here;
# they were dropped along with the gtag script, which needed consent before it
# could legally run (see src/lib/analytics.ts).
#
# Two hosts here have to match your accounts, and getting either wrong means
# the browser blocks the request silently, with no error anywhere:
#
#   * Umami Cloud needs two entries, and this is the trap: the script is
#     served from cloud.umami.is but it posts its data to gateway.umami.is.
#     Allowing only the first one loads the tracker and then blocks every
#     pageview it tries to send, which is exactly as useless as not having it
#     and much harder to notice. For Plausible, both roles are on
#     https://plausible.io; when self-hosting, use your own origin.
#   * The two Sentry ingest hosts cover both of its data regions. A CSP
#     wildcard replaces exactly the leading labels, so *.ingest.sentry.io does
#     NOT match o123.ingest.de.sentry.io - an EU-region DSN needs its own
#     entry, which is why both are listed. Getting this wrong is invisible:
#     the browser drops the request and no error appears anywhere. A
#     self-hosted Sentry needs its own origin here instead.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://cloud.umami.is; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://cloud.umami.is https://gateway.umami.is https://*.ingest.sentry.io https://*.ingest.de.sentry.io; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
